DATA VISUALIZATION & ADVANCED EXCEL

1. Charts
Charts turn numbers into visuals.
Insert → Charts
Common Types:
●	Column/Bar Chart → compare categories

●	Line Chart → show trends over time

●	Pie Chart → show proportions

●	Scatter Plot → show relationships

Example:
 Monthly sales data → Line chart to show growth.

2. Pivot Charts
Charts created from Pivot Tables.
Why useful?
●	Automatically updates when Pivot Table changes

●	Good for summaries

Example:
 Pivot Table: Sales by region
 Pivot Chart → Visual comparison of regions.

3. Dashboards
A single screen showing key information using charts, tables, KPIs.
Purpose: Quick decision-making.
Example Dashboard Shows:
●	Total Sales

●	Top Product

●	Monthly Trend

●	Region-wise performance


4. Interactive Dashboards
Dashboards where users can change filters.
Tools Used:
●	Slicers

●	Timelines

●	Dropdowns

Example:
 Click “Region = South” → All charts update.

5. Power Pivot
Advanced data modeling tool.
Used for:
●	Handling large data

●	Creating relationships between tables

●	Advanced calculations (DAX formulas)

Example:
 Link Sales table with Product table using Product ID.

6. Power Query
Tool for importing and cleaning data automatically.
Used for:
●	Importing from Excel, CSV, Web

●	Removing duplicates

●	Splitting columns

●	Transforming data

Example:
 Monthly sales files combined into one report.

DATA VISUALIZATION PRINCIPLES


1. Choosing the Right Chart
Situation	Best Chart
Compare categories	Bar/Column
Trend over time	Line
Distribution	Histogram
Relationship	Scatter

2. Data Storytelling
Using visuals to explain insights clearly.
Example Story:
 “Sales dropped in June due to low marketing but increased after promotions.”

3. Avoiding Misleading Visuals
Bad visuals can confuse.
•	Wrong Y-axis scale
•	 Too many colors
•	3D charts
•	Keep it simple and honest.

4. KPI Design (Key Performance Indicators)
KPIs measure performance.
Good KPI should be:
●	Clear

●	Measurable

●	Relevant

Examples:
●	Revenue Growth %

●	Customer Retention Rate

●	Average Delivery Time


5. Dashboard Best Practices
•	Keep it simple
•	Use consistent colors
•	Highlight key number
•	Avoid clutter
•	Use interactive filters
•	Place most important info on top

